{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Sorry, sorry. I'm after being late. The bus was a pure disaster.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): You're grand, come on in and sit yourself down. It's wild on the roads today.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): We left the flat in loads of time, doctor. The forty six just never showed.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (PATIENT): Can we not do the whole bus thing. I was stuck in that roasting waiting room and I just want to get on with it.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): Of course. What brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (PATIENT): Right. I want to sort out contraception. I'm sick of stressing about it.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Grand. What have you used before, if anything?",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (PATIENT): I was on the pill for contraception for a good while, then I came off it. Umm. Because of headaches.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (CAREGIVER): It was that packet from the chemist on Thomas Street. Ridgevidon, wasn't it? The one you showed me.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (PATIENT): Yeah, ridgevidon, for contraception. Thirty microgram. One tablet every morning, by mouth. I was on it a year-ish, maybe longer, I don't know.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Rigevidon, the thirty microgram combined pill, once every morning by mouth. And you've stopped it.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (PATIENT): Stopped it, yeah. The headaches were brutal.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): When did those headaches actually start?",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (PATIENT): Err. Last winter, or the winter before that. I genuinely cannot put a date on it.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Are they still there, or did they ease once you came off the pill?",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (PATIENT): They went once I stopped the pill. Thank god. Brutal pounding headaches in my head, most days, from last winter or the winter before. I still couldn't tell you which.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any flashing lights, zigzag lines, or weakness in an arm or a leg with them?",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): No. None of that. Just the head.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any history yourself of migraine, blood clots, or high blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (PATIENT): No. None of that.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke at all?",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (PATIENT): The odd cigarette. Weekends, like. Not every day.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (CAREGIVER): That's about right. A few on a Saturday if we're out, not through the week.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any other medicines at the minute?",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (PATIENT): No. Nothing.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Allergies to medicines, or to anything else?",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (PATIENT): No. Nothing I know of.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any chance you could be pregnant just now?",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (PATIENT): No. Not a chance.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): And the periods? Pain, or cycles all over the shop?",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (PATIENT): They're regular. No bother.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain, breathlessness, or a swollen calf?",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any operations in the past?",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (PATIENT): No. Never.",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (NURSE): I'll just take the blood pressure while ye are at it, if that's alright.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (PATIENT): Yeah, whatever. Left arm is fine.",
  "[SEG0038] person_4 (NURSE): Blood pressure is one hundred and sixteen over seventy four. Pulse is seventy six.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lovely. One sixteen over seventy four, pulse seventy six. That's grand for you.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me say it back so I have it right. You want contraception sorted, you stopped rigevidon thirty micrograms because of pounding headaches that started last winter or the winter before and you can't date it, and they settled when you stopped. You have the odd cigarette at the weekend, no allergies, no migraine or clots. Not pregnant, periods regular, and today's pressure is grand.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (PATIENT): Yeah. That's the lot. Can we not drag it all out.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): I won't drag it. Given the headaches and the smoking, I'd be slow to put you back on a combined pill. My impression is those headaches were probably down to the pill.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (PATIENT): So what am I meant to use then. I need something that actually works.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): The ones I'd think about are the progestogen-only pill, the implant, or a coil. The implant lasts three years and there's no tablet to remember.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (PATIENT): The implant sounds like a lot. Umm. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She had a leaflet half open on the bus, then she got ratty when I mentioned it.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (PATIENT): I was just looking. I didn't say I wanted the thing stuck in me.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (DOCTOR): No pressure at all. I'm giving you the implant leaflet now. Have a read in your own time, there's no decision today.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (PATIENT): Right. I'm not picking anything today. My head's not able for it.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (DOCTOR): That's perfectly fine. We won't start a thing today. Come back in three weeks and we'll decide it together.",
  "[SEG0051] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I'll ask reception to book the three weeks on the way out.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (DOCTOR): Perfect. Reception will book that review for in three weeks. Mind yourselves heading home.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (PATIENT): Grand. Finally."
 ],
